PSO state relevance
===================

Authority and scope
  Source: docs/Rendering.PsoStateRelevance.Proposal.md (approved).
  Parent: docs/PBR.BaselineShading.todo, suppress draw-irrelevant state application/restoration.
  Existing contract: docs/Rendering.AuthoritativePipelineState.md.
  Derive relevance from complete declarations and verified prepared executable information;
  retain authored intent, a single StateCache owner and exact engine-state handback.
  No renderer ignore flags, nullable intent, new geometry-adapter contract, renderer-local dirty
  tracker, shader source scanning, draw-loop driver queries or reinterpretation of partial overrides.
  Do not expand scope to texture binding caching, new sky scheduling or GPU-time optimization.

Execution and evidence
  Every task starts unchecked. Complete only when its stated evidence exists and linked documents
  agree. Use subagents for build/test tools. Follow repository comments, visibility regions,
  focused source responsibilities, existing preparation, resource lifetime and cleanup contracts.
  Use lightweight focused tests routinely; distinguish source review, CPU contracts, GPU pixels,
  exact state handback, native-call counters, canonical packaging and live appearance evidence.
  Never launch the game for visual acceptance. No absolute timing target or mandatory live gate
  is introduced by this plan; do not claim GPU/frame-time or appearance gains from headless checks.
  Preserve all unrelated work and leave the parent implementation task unchecked until acceptance.

Implementation choices and conservative bounds
  Select names and source layout through the existing pipeline/state domains. The proposal fixes
  semantics, not new public APIs or a second state owner.
  Use verified output-primitive metadata if already available through executable preparation;
  otherwise conservatively retain all affected primitive groups for geometry/tessellation shaders.
  No metadata/reflection expansion is required merely to remove more setters.
  Keep restart enables conservative because geometry adapters have no common indexing declaration.
  Preserve current boundary entry shape: include the bounded clear-helper envelope even when the
  callback ultimately uses only Preserve passes. Extra capture work is accepted; extra setters are not.
  Keep conservative application for every field without an approved irrelevance proof, including
  viewport, depth range, clip conventions/distances, provoking vertex, discard, sRGB, dither and
  logic-op disable. Preserve sampling enables even for single-sample targets.

Phase 1: Preserve declarations and derive prepared relevance
  Outcome: complete authored values and immutable relevance metadata have executable contracts;
  production application and boundary coverage remain on their existing conservative path.
  ☐ Reverify declaration, preparation and call-group ownership against current source.
    - Inspect GraphicsPipelineDesc, PipelineCanonicalization, GraphicsPipeline lifetime/preparation,
      StateCache complete application, category knowledge, PipelineStateCoverage and pass validation.
    - Record native setters that update combined fields or alias all output slots; use their actual
      write groups as the unit of relevance/coverage, distinct from declared values and validity bits.
  ☐ Preserve dormant authored intent and predictable pipeline identity.
    - Remove destructive disabled-value canonicalization for depth/stencil, raster, blend, sampling
      and assembly settings. Retain only semantically lossless representation normalization.
    - Validate all authored enums, ranges, finite values and capabilities before derivation, including
      dormant settings. Preserve structural equality/hashing, excluding labels and native identities;
      declarations with different dormant authored values remain distinct.
    - Keep declared dynamic values required and validated even when dormant. Preserve concrete
      defaults for undeclared dynamic slots; neither omitted nor skipped values inherit intent.
  ☐ Derive immutable field/group and indexed-slot relevance with prepared pipelines.
    - Derive static selectors from topology, polygon mode, enables, target aspects/formats/samples,
      sparse output slots, equations and constant-factor use. Validate against matched pass signatures.
    - Resolve emitted primitive information during preparation where verified metadata exists;
      otherwise use the conservative unknown-output path. Rebuild with executable reload/lifetime.
    - Current dynamic values do not toggle selectors. Document the future-selector rule: predeclare
      union coverage before entry and resolve the operation mask before application.
  ☐ Verify authored retention, equality/hash differences, lossless normalization, invalid dormant
    settings, explicit defaults, dynamic requirements, sparse/integer targets, emitted primitive
    fallback and reload metadata. Update obsolete canonical-equality expectations with intent checks.
  ☐ Completion: focused subagent-run contracts pass; every dependency-table row maps to a derived
    group or an explicit conservative rule, without activating sparse application prematurely.

Phase 2: Separate sparse authority from complete admission
  Depends on Phase 1. Outcome: sparse coverage and helper envelopes are verified and ready for
  coordinated activation; the existing full application still has sufficient restoration authority.
  ☐ Separate complete-graphics admission from automatic all-field coverage expansion.
    - Add sparse potential-write composition from prepared relevance while preserving complete-draw
      validation, resource footprints, context identity and rejection of undeclared operations.
    - Keep the active full-application boundary conservative until Phase 3 switches both together.
      Do not run existing unconditional setters under the new sparse authority.
    - Preserve explicit partial GlPipelineDesc/helper semantics and existing non-graphics boundaries.
  ☐ Define the bounded clear-operation envelope from RenderPassOperations.Load.
    - Include discard, sRGB, dither, scissor enable/rectangle, indexed color masks, depth write mask
      and front/back stencil write masks, expanding global aliases to all affected native slots.
    - Keep clear values as operation inputs. Clear-only contexts need helper coverage without a PSO;
      Preserve/Discard-only loads perform no clear-state application. Preserve other helper coverage.
  ☐ Refine shared coverage/query/knowledge/restoration groups where required.
    - Combined factor/equation/stencil/polygon setters cover their full actual native writes.
      Without independent blending, global factor/equation writes cover all slots and retain existing
      capability compatibility validation; sparse routes do not narrow global native effects.
    - Capture potential writes before mutation using existing known cache state where possible.
      Keep saved/current comparisons; do not introduce a new dirty tracker or invalidate whole
      categories to represent a dormant field. Preserve failure cleanup and conservative invalidation.
  ☐ Verify sparse union/Contains, indexed/global aliases, complete admission without full expansion,
    undeclared-mutation rejection, clear-only footprints and retained partial-helper behavior.
  ☐ Completion: focused subagent-run coverage/boundary checks pass; all current active setters still
    have authority, and sparse application can be enabled without missing restoration fields.

Phase 3: Apply relevant groups and activate matching boundary coverage
  Depends on Phase 2. Outcome: production complete draws leave dormant state untouched and establish
  relevant declared values, with matching potential-write restoration coverage.
  ☐ Switch complete application and boundary construction together to prepared relevance.
    - Share resolved groups across application, mutation validation and restoration coverage.
      Update any descriptor-only application paths conservatively without guessing executable output.
    - Union all declared pipelines, existing resource/binding footprints and the clear envelope at entry.
      Do not base restoration on only the final selected pipeline or last draw's relevance.
    - Skip dormant setters without modifying their cached native values or marking declarations applied.
      Retain unchanged-value suppression for relevant fields through the same existing setters.
  ☐ Implement primitive and raster dependencies.
    - Lines include polygon-mode Line. Gate line width/smoothing and compatibility stipple; stipple
      parameters require enable. Fixed point size requires points and program point size disabled.
    - Establish point-size enable and conservative sprite-origin/smoothing for point draws; gate
      polygon-only controls and applicable offset enables, with bias parameters only when applicable.
    - Gate polygon cull enable/mode appropriately; retain front-face orientation for polygons even
      with culling disabled, preserving shader facing and two-sided stencil observations.
    - Gate scissor rectangle by enable while still disabling inherited scissoring for unclipped draws.
      Keep unknown emitted primitive groups conservative and all other approved conservative fields.
  ☐ Implement depth/stencil, output, sampling and assembly dependencies.
    - Depth aspect controls depth-test enable relevance; comparison/write mask require enabled test.
      Stencil aspect controls test-enable relevance; face functions/references/ops/masks require test.
      Preserve both stencil faces and conservative depth range/clip conventions.
    - Apply color masks to routed slots regardless of blending. Apply blend enables for routed
      blendable outputs, equations when enabled, factors for factor-using equation channels, and
      blend constant only when consumed. MIN/MAX ignore factors; integer targets bypass blending.
    - Leave holes/trailing outputs untouched. When either channel requires a combined setter,
      submit all declared operands and preserve full native-call-group restoration/alias coverage.
    - Gate coverage payload, mask words and minimum shading by their enables; keep sampling enables
      conservative. Gate restart index by programmable restart without fixed-index override and
      patch vertex count by patch topology; keep restart enables conservative across adapters.
  ☐ Preserve clear/draw sequencing and exact native handback.
    - Depth/stencil clears establish write masks independently of test enables; region clears
      establish scissor independently of the following draw. Relevant draw state follows clear state.
    - Restore changed inherited parameters even if incoming features were disabled or the last draw
      leaves parameters dormant. Untouched groups emit no compensating restoration setters.
    - On setter failure invalidate the affected group, attempt restoration, continue independent
      cleanup and propagate fatal handoff failure through existing paths. Keep external invalidation.
  ☐ Verify focused GPU transitions for triangle width 2/inherited 4 → line width 2 → triangle → restore 4,
    disabled/active scissor and blend state, sparse output reuse, point-size modes and grouped writes.
    Replace unconditional-default tests with observable pixels, authored intent and exact handback;
    retain existing failure and validation strength.
  ☐ Completion: focused subagent-run CPU/GPU checks pass with relevance active; no native application
    exceeds declared authority, and no relevant feature inherits stale state.

Phase 4: Qualify correctness and native-call reductions
  Depends on Phase 3. Outcome: integrated evidence demonstrates unchanged rendering and exact handback
  while eliminating the captured unnecessary setters/restoration.
  ☐ Exercise the complete dependency/transition matrix in focused GPU fixtures.
    - Filled/wireframe/line/point and unknown geometry/tessellation outputs; culling disabled with
      front-face observations; applicable offsets and supported compatibility primitive controls.
    - Dormant-to-active depth/stencil with present/absent aspects; sampling payloads and restart/patch
      selectors; dynamic supplied/default values and invalid authored/dynamic declarations.
    - Mixed indexed blending, integer targets, sparse routes becoming active, MIN/MAX versus factor
      equations, blend constants and combined RGB/alpha writes; global fallback aliases where supported.
    - Region/color/depth/stencil clears, clear-only and Preserve-only contexts; grouped cache knowledge,
      skipped draws, shader reload, recovery, mutation failures and exact handback on failure.
  ☐ Compare representative sky/cloud/fullscreen and point-resolve workloads under matched inputs.
    - Use hostile inherited nondefault/dormant state. Compare all affected pixels and independently
      inspect complete inherited state, not only parameters relevant to the last draw.
    - Capture bounded native-call events/counters separating setup, draw application and restoration.
      Demonstrate absent line/point setters for filled fullscreen draws, absent disabled scissor-box
      normalization, and absent disabled/unrouted blend payload writes; retain necessary transitions.
    - Use small focused fixtures and a controlled test-only conservative reference if needed. Avoid
      preserving redundant production implementations or copying entire legacy shader pipelines.
  ☐ Reconcile any old tests asserting unconditional dormant defaults without deleting correctness,
    ownership or restoration coverage. Remove temporary diagnostic/reference scaffolding after its
    required comparisons are recorded; retain useful regression tests for current contracts.
  ☐ Completion: subagent-run focused regressions pass; evidence links inputs, output/state comparisons,
    call groups and measured reductions. No timing, full-driver-trace or live-appearance claim is made.

Phase 5: Reconcile contracts and qualify the canonical package
  Depends on Phase 4. Outcome: documentation, tests and packaged code describe the same accepted behavior.
  ☐ Update Rendering.AuthoritativePipelineState.md for complete observable draw control, authored
    identity, prepared relevance, sparse mutation/restoration coverage and clear-only envelopes.
    Update other affected current-state documents; retain the proposal as design authority rather
    than rewriting architecture documentation as a historical log.
  ☐ Run subagent-owned required builds, shader checks and focused Debug/Release regressions through
    canonical repository tooling; rebuild the canonical package and verify it contains the tested code.
    Record exact commands/results, configuration, source/package identity and material limitations.
  ☐ Perform a second source/plan/proposal review and resolve every uncovered dependency or unsupported
    scope change. Confirm conservative fallbacks, no renderer bypasses, exact external handoff,
    independent cleanup and no unnecessary scaffolding; leave unrelated parent tasks untouched.
  ☐ Completion: every proposal requirement has source and appropriate validation evidence, docs and
    package agree, and the parent implementation task links that evidence before being marked complete.

Final acceptance
  ☐ Complete PSOs preserve all authored values while applying only relevant native write groups.
  ☐ Dormant values/cache knowledge remain intact; later relevant draws establish intent before drawing.
  ☐ Clear operations and indexed/global aliases have sufficient independent restoration authority.
  ☐ Pixels and exact inherited state pass transition/failure checks; matched calls show reduced work.
  ☐ Canonical package, current documentation and subagent-run validation receipts agree.
